# Nintendo Switch Online SNES controller (Bluetooth), hid-nintendo driver
# (kernel night/usb-peripherals). Like Android's own Switch Pro Controller
# layout (Vendor_057e_Product_2009.kl) and the console's built-in pad, each
# button sends the key of its printed letter: A (right) = BUTTON_A, B
# (bottom) = BUTTON_B, X (top) = BUTTON_X, Y (left) = BUTTON_Y. Without this
# file Generic.kl swapped A/B and X/Y on this pad only.

# B, A, X, Y
key 0x130    BUTTON_B
key 0x131    BUTTON_A
key 0x133    BUTTON_X
key 0x134    BUTTON_Y

key 0x136    BUTTON_L1
key 0x137    BUTTON_R1
key 0x138    BUTTON_L2
key 0x139    BUTTON_R2

axis 0x10    HAT_X
axis 0x11    HAT_Y

# Minus, Plus
key 0x13a    BUTTON_SELECT
key 0x13b    BUTTON_START
